{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788372347788,"sessionID":"ses_f9cb500feffeJAzwf2KlQEhiz0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"call_dcbfa45d807e40f0959a4c76","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Explore data: distinct team names across all CSVs","priority":"high","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Implement soccer_mcp package (data_loader, queries, server)","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Create entry point server.py + requirements.txt","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Write BDD/GWT pytest suites","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Run tests, verify MCP server starts and tools respond","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Update README.md","priority":"medium","status":"pending"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Explore data: distinct team names across all CSVs\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Implement soccer_mcp package (data_loader, queries, server)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Create entry point server.py + requirements.txt\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write BDD/GWT pytest suites\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run tests, verify MCP server starts and tools respond\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update README.md\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Explore data: distinct team names across all CSVs","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement soccer_mcp package (data_loader, queries, server)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Create entry point server.py + requirements.txt","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD/GWT pytest suites","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests, verify MCP server starts and tools respond","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update README.md","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"6 todos","time":{"start":1788372347771,"end":1788372347776}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The mcp package is in `/home/retort/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages`. The MCPServer class has `tool` decorator, `run`, etc. — similar to FastMCP.\n\nNow, importantly: the core of the task is really the data query layer + tools. To make the code robust across mcp v1 (FastMCP) and v2 (MCPServer), I'll write a compatibility import:\n\n```python\ntry:\n    from mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer as Server  # mcp >= 2\nexcept ImportError:\n    from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP as Server  # mcp < 2\n```\n\nBoth support `@server.tool()` decorator and `.run()`.\n\nNow let me set up the todo list and plan the implementation:\n\nProject structure:\n```\n/workspace/\n├── soccer_mcp/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── data_loader.py    — loads all 6 CSVs into normalized Match/Player records\n│   ├── queries.py        — query functions (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)\n│   └── server.py         — MCP server exposing tools\n├── server.py             — entry point script\n├── requirements.txt\n├── tests/\n│   ├── conftest.py       — fixtures\n│   ├── test_data_loading.py\n│   ├── test_match_queries.py\n│   ├── test_team_queries.py\n│   ├── test_player_queries.py\n│   ├── test_competition_queries.py\n│   └── test_statistics.py\n├── pytest.ini or pyproject.toml (pytest config)\n└── README.md (updated)\n```\n\nKey design decisions:\n\n1. **Data model**: Normalize all matches into a common `Match` dataclass: date (ISO), competition, season, round/stage, home_team, away_team, home_goals, away_goals, source_file. Normalize team names (strip state suffixes like \"-SP\", \" (RJ)\", etc.), unify accents handling (NFKD normalization for matching).\n\n2. **Team name normalization**: \n   - \"Palmeiras-SP\" -> \"Palmeiras\"\n   - \"América - MG\" -> \"América\" (note: in Brazilian_Cup_Matches it's \"América - MG\" with spaces)\n   - Full names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" -> harder. The fifa data uses names like \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"? Let me check. FIFA club names... Let me check what club names are in fifa_data.\n   - Also BR-Football-Dataset uses \"Sao Paulo\" (without accents!). So need accent-insensitive matching.\n\n3. **Matching approach**: Build a canonical name map. For each raw team name, compute a \"key\": lowercase, strip accents (unicodedata NFKD, remove combining), remove state suffixes, remove common words like \"sport club\", \"ec\", \"fc\", punctuation, etc. Then match teams by key.\n\nLet me think about the specific data:\n\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\" — suffix `-UF`.\n- Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\", \"América - MG\" — suffix \" - UF\" and parenthetical stuff.\n- Libertadores_Matches.csv: \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Boca Juniors\" — country suffixes in parens or after dash for foreign teams. \"Barcelona-EQU\" is Barcelona of Ecuador. Hmm, tricky. \"Flamengo\" would appear without suffix probably. Let me check.\n- BR-Football-Dataset.csv: \"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\" — plain names, no accents on \"Sao Paulo\" apparently.\n- novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv: \"Guarani\", \"Vasco\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Grêmio\" — mixed.\n- fifa_data.csv: Club names like \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"? Need to check.\n\nNormalization function plan:\n```python\ndef normalize_team_name(raw):\n    s = raw.strip()\n    # remove parenthetical content: \"Nacional (URU)\" -> \"Nacional\", \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo ...) - RJ\" -> \"Boavista Sport Club - RJ\"\n    s = re.sub(r'\\(.*?\\)', '', s)\n    # remove state/country suffix: \" - RJ\" or \"-SP\" or \"-EQU\" (2-3 letters at end)\n    s = re.sub(r'[\\s\\-]+[A-Z]{2,3}$', '', s)  # careful with case\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm wait, \"América - MG\": the suffix is \" - MG\". \"Palmeiras-SP\": \"-SP\". \"Barcelona-EQU\": \"-EQU\". But also plain names might end with capital letters... like \"CRB\"? Actually CRB is a team (Clube de Regatas Brasil). If I strip \"-AL\" from \"CRB-AL\" I get \"CRB\" which is fine. But what about \"Gama-DF\" -> \"Gama\". OK.\n\nEdge cases: teams like \"ABC\" (RN team)? \"ABC-RN\" -> \"ABC\". The regex `[\\s-]+[A-Z]{2,3}$` on \"ABC-RN\" strips \"-RN\" leaving \"ABC\". Good. But what about just \"ABC\"? The regex would strip... \"ABC\" matches `[A-Z]{2,3}$` but requires `[\\s\\-]+` before it, so plain \"ABC\" is untouched. Good. What about \"Atlético-GO\"? -> \"Atlético\". Good.\n\nBut careful: \"Sport-PE\" -> \"Sport\". \"Sport\" is the team name (Sport Club do Recife). Good.\n\nThen canonical key: lowercase, remove accents, remove punctuation, remove filler words (sport club, ec, fc, sc, clube de regatas...). Hmm, that's risky. Let me keep it simpler:\n\nkey = lowercase, NFKD strip accents, remove non-alphanumeric, strip state suffix, then also remove common noise words for matching: \"sport club\", \"futebol clube\", \"ec\", \"fc\", \"sc\", \"sp fc\"? Hmm.\n\nActually for the FIFA club names, let me check what Brazilian club names appear in the fifa_data. Let me look.\n\nAlso common name mappings (a curated alias map) is the pragmatic approach used widely:\n- \"Corinthians\": [\"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\", \"SC Corinthians Paulista\"]\n- \"São Paulo\": [\"Sao Paulo\", \"SPFC\"]\n- \"Athletico-PR\": [\"Atlético-PR\", \"Atletico Paranaense\"...]\n\nLet me inspect the data to see what actual variants exist. Let me write a quick exploration script.\n\nActually, let me be pragmatic. I'll build a normalization pipeline:\n\n1. Strip parentheticals.\n2. Strip trailing state/country suffix patterns: `-XX`, ` - XX`, `-XXX`.\n3. Lowercase + strip accents + remove non-letters.\n4. Alias map for known canonical names (curated after inspecting data).\n\nFor matching, compare normalized keys. Build a union of all names across files mapping key -> canonical display name.\n\nLet me explore the distinct team names across the files first. Also need to check FIFA Club values for Brazilian clubs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634c64fc001PaoTPesbKksaxj","sessionID":"ses_f9cb500feffeJAzwf2KlQEhiz0","messageID":"msg_0634c00ab001ZZKRjuYfSnJIym"}}
