{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788372449899,"sessionID":"ses_f9cb500feffeJAzwf2KlQEhiz0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_6dc82a88b787436191df5a57","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nseasons = defaultdict(Counter)\nwith open('/workspace/data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        seasons[r['tournament']][r['date'][:4]] += 1\nfor t, c in seasons.items():\n    print(t, dict(sorted(c.items())))\nEOF"},"output":"Copa do Brasil {'2014': 43, '2015': 139, '2016': 147, '2017': 105, '2018': 111, '2019': 117, '2020': 117, '2021': 111, '2022': 117, '2023': 116}\nSerie A {'2014': 281, '2015': 378, '2016': 379, '2017': 380, '2018': 380, '2019': 380, '2020': 264, '2021': 491, '2022': 379, '2023': 377}\nSerie B {'2014': 275, '2015': 378, '2016': 380, '2017': 381, '2018': 377, '2019': 378, '2020': 302, '2021': 446, '2022': 380, '2023': 380}\nSerie C {'2014': 81, '2015': 157, '2016': 181, '2017': 179, '2018': 192, '2019': 194, '2020': 179, '2021': 216, '2022': 213, '2023': 215}\n","metadata":{"output":"Copa do Brasil {'2014': 43, '2015': 139, '2016': 147, '2017': 105, '2018': 111, '2019': 117, '2020': 117, '2021': 111, '2022': 117, '2023': 116}\nSerie A {'2014': 281, '2015': 378, '2016': 379, '2017': 380, '2018': 380, '2019': 380, '2020': 264, '2021': 491, '2022': 379, '2023': 377}\nSerie B {'2014': 275, '2015': 378, '2016': 380, '2017': 381, '2018': 377, '2019': 378, '2020': 302, '2021': 446, '2022': 380, '2023': 380}\nSerie C {'2014': 81, '2015': 157, '2016': 181, '2017': 179, '2018': 192, '2019': 194, '2020': 179, '2021': 216, '2022': 213, '2023': 215}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nseasons = defaultdict(Counter)\nwith open('/workspace/data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        seasons[r['tournament']][r['date'][:4]] += 1\nfor t, c in seasons.items():\n    print(t, dict(sorted(c.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788372449888,"end":1788372449895}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Confirmed: the two Brasileirão files overlap for 2012-2019 (2019: 305/380 exact duplicates — some differ due to name/date formatting nuances, but they're the same matches).\n\nStrategy: treat the two files as two sources but dedupe when computing standings/queries. Approach options:\n\n**Option A**: Merge into a single \"Brasileirão Serie A\" competition, deduping by (date, home_key, away_key). For seasons 2012-2019 there will be ~75 matches/season that don't dedupe exactly (due to date or name normalization differences — e.g. \"avai\" from \"Avaí-SC\"... hmm both normalize to 'avai', dates might differ due to time or postponed matches). Let me check what the non-overlapping ones look like. 380+380-305 = 455 unique for 2019 → 75 extra. That's bad for standings (each team would have extra games).\n\nBetter dedup key: (season, home_key, away_key) — each pair plays exactly twice per season (home and away). For 2019 Serie A, 20 teams → 380 matches, each pair meets twice. So dedup by (season, home_key, away_key) plus round? Round numbers should align. Let me test dedup by (season, home_key, away_key) and see how many dupes remain.\n\n**Option B**: Keep the sources separate but have queries use only Brasileirao_Matches for 2012+ and the historical file only for 2003-2011. That's cleaner: \"Brasileirão Serie A\" competition = historical 2003-2011 + Brasileirao_Matches 2012-2022. Wait, but Brasileirao_Matches ends at 2022 (380 matches per season 2012-2022 = 4180). Hmm, spec said example \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" — but data has no 2023 Brasileirão? The Cup file also ends at 2021. BR-FD probably has 2023. Whatever — queries return what's in the data.\n\nLet me verify option B dedup: for seasons 2012-2019 prefer Brasileirao_Matches (more recent, canonical), use hist for 2003-2011. But wait — the BR-FD \"Serie A\" tournament also covers some years! 3689 Serie A matches. Let me check its seasons: if it's 2018-2023, then for Serie A 2018-2022 there's overlap with Brasileirao_Matches. But BR-FD has the richer stats (corners etc.) and possibly 2023.\n\nHmm, this is getting complex. Let me define competitions from sources:\n- \"Brasileirão Serie A\": merge of hist (2003-2011) + Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022) + BR-FD Serie A? Let me check BR-FD Serie A seasons first.\n- \"Copa do Brasil\": Brazilian_Cup_Matches (2012-2021) + BR-FD Copa do Brasil (1123 matches — overlapping years?).\n- \"Libertadores\": Libertadores file 2013-2022.\n- \"Serie B\", \"Serie C\": only from BR-FD.\n\nI need to check BR-FD seasons per tournament.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634df61b0014JskivoVwgPSiY","sessionID":"ses_f9cb500feffeJAzwf2KlQEhiz0","messageID":"msg_0634dbe6e0019jRkh03ODksyWC"}}
