]))].append(('BM', r['home_goal'], r['away_goal']))\nwith open('/workspace/data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        m[(r['Ano'], norm(r['Equipe_mandante']), norm(r['Equipe_visitante']))].append(('HIST', r['Gols_mandante'], r['Gols_visitante']))\n\ndup = 0; conflict = 0\nfor k, v in m.items():\n    if len(v) > 1:\n        dup += 1\n        scores = {(a,b) for _,a,b in v}\n        if len(scores) > 1:\n            conflict += 1\n            if conflict < 8: print(\"CONFLICT\", k, v)\nprint(\"dup keys:\", dup, \"conflicts:\", conflict)\nprint(\"total unique (season,home,away):\", len(m))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788372465401,"end":1788372465417}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"BR-FD covers 2014-2023 for Serie A/B/C and Copa do Brasil. There's overlap with Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022) and Cup file (2012-2021). The BR-FD data has unique extras: 2023 Serie A, plus detailed stats (corners, shots, attacks).\n\nData quality in BR-FD: 2020 Serie A only 264, 2021 has 491 (duplicated?). Whatever.\n\nMerge strategy per competition:\n- **\"Brasileirão Serie A\"**: hist(2003-2011) + Brasileirao_Matches(2012-2022) + BR-FD Serie A(2023 only? or those not duplicating). To avoid dupes, I'll dedupe by (season, date, home_key, away_key) and prefer... hmm, actually simpler: for a (season, home_key, away_key) pair, teams play twice. But BR-FD has team names without state and full matches per season too.\n\nSimplest robust approach for standings/queries: **dedupe by (season, home_key, away_key, home_goals, away_goals)** across merged sources? If both files recorded the same match, date+score same → dedupe. Differences: hist has date dd/mm/yyyy, round numbers align. In 2019 the overlap was 305/380 by (date,home,away,score). The other 75 differ probably due to date differences (postponed matches recorded with different dates) or scores mismatch... Let me not overthink: dedupe by (season, home_key, away_key, home_goals, away_goals) — each pair-home-away happens once per season, score fixed. That should collapse near-dupes. Check: 2019 → how many unique after this dedup? If it's 380, perfect.\n\nActually even better: dedupe by (season, home_key, away_key) — in a double round-robin, each (home, away) pairing occurs exactly once per season. For Serie A 2012-2022 that's exact. Risk: rescheduled matches or data errors could break it, but if both files give a (season, home, away) the scores should be the same match. When scores conflict, prefer the source with higher priority (Brasileirao_Matches > BR-FD > hist? or hist > brasileirao?). In 2019, 305 exact dupes; 75 not exact. With (season, home, away) key, dupes = ?\n\nLet me test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634e25b2001m5aned62juTe7k","sessionID":"ses_f9cb500feffeJAzwf2KlQEhiz0","messageID":"msg_0634dfaf9001pfYVYGeEnVKTJa"}}
