{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788372645874,"sessionID":"ses_f9cb500feffeJAzwf2KlQEhiz0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_5c8d8bb1d98d4a6c86fefb1d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\ndef strip_accents(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\nALIASES = {\n    'atleticomineiro': ('atletico','MG'), 'atleticoparanaense': ('atletico','PR'),\n    'athleticoparanaense': ('atletico','PR'), 'atleticogoianiense': ('atletico','GO'),\n    'sportrecife': ('sport','PE'), 'sportclubdorecife': ('sport','PE'),\n    'cearasportingclub': ('ceara','CE'), 'vascodagamarj': ('vascodagama','RJ'),\n    'vascodagama': ('vascodagama','RJ'), 'sccorinthianspaulista': ('corinthians','SP'),\n    'sportclubcorinthianspaulista': ('corinthians','SP'),\n}\nBASE_FIXES = {'athletico': 'atletico'}\n\ndef parse(name):\n    s = name.strip()\n    region = ''\n    m = re.search(r'\\(\\s*([A-Za-z]{2,3})\\s*\\)\\s*$', s)\n    if m: region = m.group(1).upper(); s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n    m = re.search(r'[\\s\\-]+([A-Za-z]{2,3})$', s)\n    if m and m.group(1).isupper():\n        region = region or m.group(1).upper(); s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n    base = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]', '', strip_accents(s.lower()))\n    base = BASE_FIXES.get(base, base)\n    if base in ALIASES and not region:\n        base, region = ALIASES[base]\n    return base, region\n\ndef parse_date(d):\n    d = (d or '').strip()\n    for fmt in ('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S','%Y-%m-%d','%d/%m/%Y'):\n        try: return datetime.strptime(d, fmt).date().isoformat()\n        except ValueError: pass\n    return None\n\n# phase 1: collect region counts\nregion_counts = defaultdict(Counter)\ndef collect(path, cols):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols:\n                b, rg = parse(r[c])\n                region_counts[b][rg] += 1\n\nfor path, cols in [\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', ['home','away']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', ['Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante']),\n]:\n    collect(path, cols)\n\ndef canonical(name):\n    base, region = parse(name)\n    if not region:\n        region = region_counts[base].most_common(1)[0][0] if region_counts[base] else ''\n    return base + region.lower()\n\n# phase 2: load & dedupe\nrows = []\ndef add(path, comp, hcol, acol, hg, ag, dcol, scol=None):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            d = parse_date(r[dcol])\n            s = r[scol] if scol else (d[:4] if d else None)\n            rows.append((comp, s, canonical(r[hcol]), canonical(r[acol]), r[hg], r[ag], d))\n\nadd('/workspace/data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','Serie A','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime','season')\nadd('/workspace/data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Serie A','Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante','Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante','Data','Ano')\nadd('/workspace/data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv','Serie A','home','away','home_goal','away_goal','date',None)\n\nfor yr in ['2003','2012','2015','2019','2021','2023']:\n    sub = [r for r in rows if r[1]==yr]\n    key = Counter((r[2],r[3],r[6],r[4],r[5]) for r in sub)\n    print(\"Serie A\", yr, \"raw:\", len(sub), \"-> dedup:\", len(key))\nEOF"},"output":"Serie A 2003 raw: 552 -> dedup: 552\nSerie A 2012 raw: 760 -> dedup: 740\nSerie A 2015 raw: 1812 -> dedup: 1806\nSerie A 2019 raw: 1829 -> dedup: 1817\nSerie A 2021 raw: 1644 -> dedup: 1644\nSerie A 2023 raw: 1088 -> dedup: 1088\n","metadata":{"output":"Serie A 2003 raw: 552 -> dedup: 552\nSerie A 2012 raw: 760 -> dedup: 740\nSerie A 2015 raw: 1812 -> dedup: 1806\nSerie A 2019 raw: 1829 -> dedup: 1817\nSerie A 2021 raw: 1644 -> dedup: 1644\nSerie A 2023 raw: 1088 -> dedup: 1088\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\ndef strip_accents(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\nALIASES = {\n    'atleticomineiro': ('atletico','MG'), 'atleticoparanaense': ('atletico','PR'),\n    'athleticoparanaense': ('atletico','PR'), 'atleticogoianiense': ('atletico','GO'),\n    'sportrecife': ('sport','PE'), 'sportclubdorecife': ('sport','PE'),\n    'cearasportingclub': ('ceara','CE'), 'vascodagamarj': ('vascodagama','RJ'),\n    'vascodagama': ('vascodagama','RJ'), 'sccorinthianspaulista': ('corinthians','SP'),\n    'sportclubcorinthianspaulista': ('corinthians','SP'),\n}\nBASE_FIXES = {'athletico': 'atletico'}\n\ndef parse(name):\n    s = name.strip()\n    region = ''\n    m = re.search(r'\\(\\s*([A-Za-z]{2,3})\\s*\\)\\s*$', s)\n    if m: region = m.group(1).upper(); s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n    m = re.search(r'[\\s\\-]+([A-Za-z]{2,3})$', s)\n    if m and m.group(1).isupper():\n        region = region or m.group(1).upper(); s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n    base = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]', '', strip_accents(s.lower()))\n    base = BASE_FIXES.get(base, base)\n    if base in ALIASES and not region:\n        base, region = ALIASES[base]\n    return base, region\n\ndef parse_date(d):\n    d = (d or '').strip()\n    for fmt in ('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S','%Y-%m-%d','%d/%m/%Y'):\n        try: return datetime.strptime(d, fmt).date().isoformat()\n        except ValueError: pass\n    return None\n\n# phase 1: collect region counts\nregion_counts = defaultdict(Counter)\ndef collect(path, cols):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols:\n                b, rg = parse(r[c])\n                region_counts[b][rg] += 1\n\nfor path, cols in [\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', ['home','away']),\n    ('/workspace/data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', ['Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante']),\n]:\n    collect(path, cols)\n\ndef canonical(name):\n    base, region = parse(name)\n    if not region:\n        region = region_counts[base].most_common(1)[0][0] if region_counts[base] else ''\n    return base + region.lower()\n\n# phase 2: load & dedupe\nrows = []\ndef add(path, comp, hcol, acol, hg, ag, dcol, scol=None):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            d = parse_date(r[dcol])\n            s = r[scol] if scol else (d[:4] if d else None)\n            rows.append((comp, s, canonical(r[hcol]), canonical(r[acol]), r[hg], r[ag], d))\n\nadd('/workspace/data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','Serie A','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime','season')\nadd('/workspace/data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Serie A','Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante','Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante','Data','Ano')\nadd('/workspace/data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv','Serie A','home','away','home_goal','away_goal','date',None)\n\nfor yr in ['2003','2012','2015','2019','2021','2023']:\n    sub = [r for r in rows if r[1]==yr]\n    key = Counter((r[2],r[3],r[6],r[4],r[5]) for r in sub)\n    print(\"Serie A\", yr, \"raw:\", len(sub), \"-> dedup:\", len(key))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788372645848,"end":1788372645864}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There it is. BM uses \"Sao Paulo-SP\" (no accent!) while HIST uses \"São Paulo\" (accent, no state). My normalization strips accents and state → both \"saopaulo\"... but earlier dedup failed because in prototype 2, \"São Paulo\" (no state) → base 'saopaulo', region '' → key 'saopaulo' while \"Sao Paulo-SP\" → 'saopaulosp'... wait no. Look at my parse() in prototype 2: region extracted from trailing uppercase suffix: \"Sao Paulo-SP\" → strips \"-SP\" → region='SP', base='saopaulo' → returns 'saopaulosp'. But \"São Paulo\" → no region → 'saopaulo'. MISMATCH: 'saopaulosp' != 'saopaulo'.\n\nThat's the flaw: stateless names don't match state'd names. I need the resolution step: canonical key should be base+state, and stateless variants must be resolved via prominence (most matches with that base). So:\n1. First pass: collect all (base, region) pairs with match counts.\n2. For each base, if exactly one (base, region) exists → that's canonical for all stateless names too.\n3. If multiple regions for same base: resolve stateless by prominence (max matches).\n\nFor \"sao paulo\": only saopaulo-SP exists in match data → 'saopaulo' → 'saopaulosp'. ✓\nFor \"flamengo\": flamengo-RJ (many) and flamengo-PI (few) → stateless \"Flamengo\" → flamengo-RJ. ✓\nFor \"avai\": avai-SC only ✓. \"Atletico-MG\" has state ✓.\n\nBut careful: BR-FD stateless \"Atletico Mineiro\" → alias → atletico+MG ✓. BR-FD \"Avai\" → avai + stateless → resolves to avaisc ✓. BM \"Atletico-MG\" → atleticomg ✓, HIST \"Atlético-MG\" → atleticomg ✓. \n\nAlso note: HIST \"Atlético-MG\" vs HIST \"Athletico-PR\" — different bases ('atletico' vs 'athletico')! Earlier group listing showed 'athleticoparanaense' and 'atletico' groups separate: 'Athletico-PR' normalized to base 'athletico' region PR. And BM has \"Atletico-PR\"? In BM 2019, teams are Atletico-MG... what about Paranaense in BM? Earlier group: 'athletico' => ['Athletico', 'Athletico-PR'] and 'atletico' => [...many 'Atlético-PR'...]. So one file spells \"Athletico-PR\" (correct since 2019 rename) and others \"Atlético-PR\". Need alias: base 'athletico' → ('atletico', 'PR')?? No wait — 'athleticoparanaense' → atletico-PR alias handles the full name, but plain \"Athletico-PR\" → base 'athletico' + PR. I need alias 'athletico' → ('atletico','PR')? But then \"Athletico-PR\" → atleticopr ✓ and plain \"Athletico\" (no state, seen in groups) → atleticopr ✓. But what if some team is \"Athletico\" something else? Unlikely. OK, add alias 'athletico' → atletico-PR. Hmm wait, actually careful: 'Athletico Paranaense' base = 'athleticoparanaense' → alias to ('atletico','PR') ✓. And 'athletico' + region PR → base 'athletico'... I should ALSO map base 'athletico' to 'atletico' regardless of region? Simplest: add 'athletico' as alternate spelling of base 'atletico' (when followed by PR region it's Paranaense). Actually simpler approach: canonical base mapping applied AFTER region extraction: if base == 'athletico' → base = 'atletico' (keep region). Then \"Athletico-PR\" → atletico+PR ✓. And alias 'athleticoparanaense'/'atleticoparanaense' → ('atletico','PR') ✓.\n\nSimilarly \"atletico\" in BR-FD... BR-FD uses full names (Atletico Mineiro etc.) so fine.\n\nWhat about \"atletico\" plain in HIST? E.g. 2003-2007: \"Atlético-PR\" and \"Atlético-MG\" both have states in HIST. OK.\n\nNow the dedup: BM \"Avai-SC\" → 'avai'+'SC' → 'avaisc'; HIST \"Avaí\" → 'avai' stateless → resolve prominence → avaisc ✓. Dates now both ISO ✓. Scores match ✓. So dedup should work. The remaining mismatch in prototype 2 was just the region-less issue.\n\nPlan the canonical resolution properly:\n\n```\nclass TeamNormalizer:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.region_counts = defaultdict(Counter)  # base -> Counter(region)\n    \n    parse_raw(name) -> (base, region)   # with aliases\n    \n    canonical(name) -> key = base + region (lowercased)\n    resolve(base, region=None):\n        # if region given: base+region\n        # else: pick region with